  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the exact value of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-{105}^{\u2218})?$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-{105}^{\u2218}={30}^{\u2218}-{135}^{\u2218}.$*",
  "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-y)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x={30}^{\u2218}$ and $y={135}^{\u2218},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-{105}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}-{135}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{135}^{\u2218}-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{135}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
